2. Content (CC BY-NC 4.0)
-------------------------
The original stories ("Lantern Original"), articles, retellings and adaptations
("Lantern Editorial"), quizzes, phrase lists, glossaries and the English-Turkish
dictionary (content/ and data/) are licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
You may share and adapt them for non-commercial purposes with credit to
"emjn / Lantern English". Commercial use, including training or building a
commercial product, requires written permission from the author.

Classic texts come from Project Gutenberg and are in the public domain (see the
Sources list on the "Nasıl Çalışır" page). Only Lantern's own retelling,
glossaries, phrases and quizzes around them fall under this section.

External films and subtitles
---------------------------
The licenses above do not apply to the externally licensed films or their
English caption text. Each video retains its own attribution and source links:
  - Sintel and Tears of Steel: Blender Foundation, CC BY 3.0.
  - Elephants Dream: Blender Foundation / Netherlands Media Art Institute,
    CC BY 2.5 (https://orange.blender.org/blog/creative-commons-license-2/).
  - Cosmos Laundromat: Blender Foundation, CC BY 3.0
    (https://gooseberry.blender.org/license/).
  - Sprite Fright and its official English captions: Blender Foundation,
    CC BY 1.0 (https://studio.blender.org/projects/sprite-fright/pages/about/).

Elephants Dream and Cosmos Laundromat English captions are credited to
Wikimedia Commons contributors and distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/TimedText:Elephants_Dream.ogv.en.srt
https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/TimedText:Cosmos_Laundromat_-_First_Cycle_-_Official_Blender_Foundation_release.webm.en-gb.srt
Authors are listed in the linked pages' revision histories. Caption words are
retained; formatting is stripped and timings converted to seconds. Three
Elephants Dream cue endings are clipped by 3-9 milliseconds to remove overlap.
These captions, including this formatting/timing conversion, remain under
CC BY-SA 4.0, separately from Lantern's original code and editorial material.
The films are played unchanged from Blender's external host, including credits.